. * GENERATE VARIABLES *
. 
. * Dependent variable: percentage of housework by men in the household.
. * We need to compute the number of hours on housework per week by adding hour
> s of 
. * housework over the week (pli0012_h: Saturday, pli0016_h: Sunday, pli0043_h:
>  day week)
. 
.         replace pli0012_h = .   if pli0012_h <0 
(7,241 real changes made, 7,241 to missing)

.         replace pli0016_h = .   if pli0016_h <0 
(7,577 real changes made, 7,577 to missing)

.         replace pli0043_h = .   if pli0043_h <0 
(2,841 real changes made, 2,841 to missing)

. 
.         gen     housework_pid           = pli0012_h + pli0016_h + 5*pli0043_h
>  
(7,766 missing values generated)

.         by              cid syear, sort: egen housework_cid = sum(housework_p
> id)

.         gen     housework_partner       = housework_cid - housework_pid
(7,766 missing values generated)

. 
.         gen     phmale = housework_pid / housework_cid if sex == 1
(38,809 missing values generated)

.         
.         * Age: We use year of birth to generate age 
.         gen     age  = syear - gebjahr

.         gen             age2 = (age * age) / 100

.         
.         
.         * Replace missing values for non-valid responses to control variable 
> (level of in education, net labour income...)
.         replace pgisced11 = .   if      pgisced11 <= 0
(8,265 real changes made, 8,265 to missing)

.         replace pglabnet = .    if  pglabnet  <= 0
(28,226 real changes made, 28,226 to missing)

. 
.         *Generate dummy for full-time job
.         gen     fulltime = 0 

.         replace fulltime = 1 if pgemplst == 1
(25,794 real changes made)

.         
.         * Generate the variables for the partner in the same row
.         by cid syear, sort: egen totage = sum(age)

.         by cid syear, sort: egen totedu = sum(pgisced11)

.         by cid syear, sort: egen totincome = sum(pglabnet)

.         by cid syear, sort: egen totfull = sum(fulltime)

.         
.         gen     age_partner     = totage-age

.         gen     edu_partner     = totedu - pgisced11
(8,265 missing values generated)

.         gen     inc_partner     = totincome - pglabnet
(28,226 missing values generated)

.         gen     full_partner    = totfull-fulltime

. 
.         gen             share_income   = pglabnet/totincome
(28,226 missing values generated)

.         
.         gen     age_partner_2   = (age_partner * age_partner)/100

.         
.         keep if sex==1
(34,575 observations deleted)

.         
.         
.         
.         
. * HYPOTHESIS TEST FOR H3 * 
. 
. * We conduct our analysis running panel data fixed effects at the household l
> evel 
. * Our dependent variable is the percertage of housework by men in the housego
> ld (phmen)
. * The set of independent variable includes age, age2, level ofd education, pe
> rcentage of
. * net labor income earned by husband, employment status (dummies for full-tim
> e), total 
. * number of hours devoted to housework in the household (housework_cid) and y
> ear dummies 
. * We include fixed effects at the household level (cid)
. 
.         xtset cid syear

Panel variable: cid (unbalanced)
 Time variable: syear, 2009 to 2019, but with gaps
         Delta: 1 unit

.         xtreg phmale d_daughter age age2 age_partner age_partner_2 pgisced11 
> edu_partner share_income fulltime full_partner housework_cid  i.syear , fe cl
> uster(cid)

